tugging. twisting. but it never hurts me. not really. not anymore.

this is what they called the woman who walked away: a hundred years ago, the world was shocked by the brutal assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand and his wife, Sophie Chotek. This was the start of WWI. But, in many ways, it was just the beginning….

On June 28, 1914, a Serbian nationalist named Gavrilo Princip shot Archduke Francis Ferdinand of Austria and his pregnant wife, Sophie, as their car passed through the streets of Sarajevo, Bosnia, then part of the Austro-Hungarian Empire. Their deaths triggered the events which led to the start of World War I, one of the bloodiest and most momentous conflicts in history. In August, Germany declared war on Serbia;
